<section aria-labelledby="general">
  <h2 id="general">1. General</h2>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:scope) %>">1.1 What belongs on HiFi&thinsp;Log</h3>
  <p>
    HiFi&thinsp;Log is a database for home hi-fi, both vintage and modern: sources, amplifiers,
    speakers, headphones, cables, accessories and DIY kits. Studio, professional and PA equipment
    does not belong here.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are not sure, ask: was the product sold to home users? Studio monitors that the
    brand also sold for home use can be added.
  </p>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:sources) %>">1.2 Sources</h3>
  <p>Use the best source that you have. From best to least good:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Documents of the brand: user manual, service manual, specification sheet, original brochure, website of the brand.</li>
    <li>Official distributors and importers of the brand. They often publish the specification sheet of the brand, and for some brands they are the only source.</li>
    <li>Test reports and reviews from the time of the product, for example in hi-fi magazines.</li>
    <li>The product itself, for example the label on the rear panel.</li>
    <li>Listings of dealers. They are good sources for the price and for the dates when the product was available. Use their specifications only if a second source confirms them: dealers often type values by hand, mix up the specifications of different models or use the same template for all products.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Try to avoid other hi-fi databases, forums, second-hand listings and AI tools as sources.
    Their data is often copied from each other and it is often wrong. If you use them, compare
    the data with a second source and write in the comment where it comes from.
  </p>
  <p>
    If two sources do not agree, use the better source. Write the difference in the comment
    (see <a href="#<%= guideline_anchor(:comments) %>">1.5</a>).
  </p>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:duplicates) %>">1.3 Duplicates and errors</h3>
  <p>
    Before you add a brand or a product, search for its name and its model number.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you find two entries for the same brand or product, or an error that you can not correct
    yourself, send an email with the links to the entries to
    <%= contact_email_link %>.
    Do not rename or empty an entry to remove it.
  </p>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:partial) %>">1.4 Incomplete information</h3>
  <p>
    You do not have to fill in all fields. Fields marked "optional" can be filled in later, by you
    or by other contributors. If you only know the year, or the year and the month, leave the
    other date fields empty.
  </p>
  <p>
    An empty field means "unknown". A wrong value is worse than an empty field, because nobody
    can see that it is wrong.
  </p>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:comments) %>">1.5 Comments on your changes</h3>
  <p>
    When you edit an entry, write in the comment what you changed and where the information comes
    from. For example: <i>"Corrected the output power. Source: user manual, page 12."</i>
    This helps other contributors to check your change and makes it less likely that it is changed
    back.
  </p>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:language) %>">1.6 Language and spelling</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Write in English.</li>
    <li>
      If the brand uses a name in a non-Latin script (for example Japanese), use the name in
      Latin letters that the brand uses, for example on export models or on its international
      website. You can add the name in the original script to the description.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:objectivity) %>">1.7 Objectivity</h3>
  <p>
    HiFi&thinsp;Log is a reference, not an advertisement. Do not use marketing words like
    <i>"legendary"</i> or <i>"best in its class"</i>, do not write your personal opinion, and do not
    add links to shops. Your opinion is welcome in your notes, not in the catalogue.
  </p>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:conduct) %>">1.8 Conduct</h3>
  <p>
    Do not add information that you know is wrong, and do not remove correct information. If you
    undo a change of another contributor, write the reason in the comment.
  </p>
</section>
